    "body": "Merged `main` (8e176ae), resolved as the review suggested:\n- The `PostProgramDialog` arm is main's `self.post_program_dialog()` (`state_per_op.rs`).\n- Its single-file branch now calls `super::post_program_dialog(&target)` with `target = post_file::for_document(self)`, and the per-operation folder picker opens at `target.dir` too (`set_directory`), so both outputs start where the document last posted.\n- No other caller of a no-argument `post_program_dialog()` is left: `grep` finds only the arm and that branch.\n\nOn `Refs #258`: yes, `Refs` on purpose. This is part 1 of the split in #258's triage (the output file); program number, per-post properties and the rest stay open there.\n\nRe-ran on the merge (sources touched first; the five `post_file` tests listed as compiled): ui lib 305 pass, 2 ignored, plus `boundary`, `boundary_picks`, `feedback`, `fixtures`, `gpu_render`, `machine`, `models`, `operations`, `shell` (92 pass). The only failures are the three pixel snapshots, same counts as clean `main` on this machine. Clippy (ui) clean. The native file and folder dialogs themselves can't run headless, so they weren't exercised. Ready again.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
